                                                "sense_id": "5459fb24-08e3-3be4-a194-da70d4c4f03e",
                                                "text": "How to take life from that dead-liuing swaine, / Whom still he marked freshly to arize / From th'earth, & from her wombe new spirits to reprize."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec0224c9-da25-3d3a-b7c2-3e64e5705ccf",
                                        "entry_id": "b75034a8-1a68-38ca-9830-86386be67c31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To repeat or resume an action or a role."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8e89e7b-f275-4b9d-8db6-5eea788e02de",
                                                "sense_id": "ec0224c9-da25-3d3a-b7c2-3e64e5705ccf",
                                                "text": "The aging actress played the role she played in her youth, as if to reprise it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0575fa5-eb99-4f58-bda0-fa91597180d0",
                                                "sense_id": "ec0224c9-da25-3d3a-b7c2-3e64e5705ccf",
                                                "text": "The notion of a \"psychological wage\" originated with Du Bois, was later employed by Fredrickson, and has been reprised in the context of northern industrialism by Roediger."
